  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Rights Movement Building in South and Southeast Asia 2024-2027</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Digital Rights Movement Building in South and Southeast Asia 2024-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EngageMedia is a non-profit organisation which promotes digital rights, open and secure technology, and social issue documentary. Combining video, technology, knowledge, and networks, EngageMedia supports Asia-Pacific and global changemakers advocating for human rights, democracy, and the environment. In collaboration with diverse networks and communities, EngageMedia defends and advances digital rights. 

The proposed budget is total US$ 2,166,100, approximately SEK 23,000,000 for 3 year programmes - Year 1 US$660,642, Year 2 US$745,666, and Year 3 US$759,791. EngageMedia&apos;s analysis shows that the human rights community in the Asia-Pacific is working amidst a backdrop of large-scale disinformation, rising authoritarianism, intensified surveillance, increased censorship, and surging violent extremism, all exacerbated by advancing unregulated machine learning, increasing weaponization of cyber laws, and weakening democratic institutions. These issues were emphasized across EngageMedia&apos;s range of initiatives. To counter digital authoritarianism and the closure of civic spaces, EngageMedia seeks support to contribute to: 

1) Greater freedoms for change-seekers, change-makers and filmmakers for climate justice and digital rights; 2) Greater understanding for civil society organizations (CSOs) to engage in public policy development, particularly in countering disinformation, platform accountability, and AI governance; 3) Greater solidarity among digital rights CSOs; and 4) Greater security for human rights defenders through the adoption and development of open and secure technologies.
EngageMedia also requests support to develop and implement an updated strategy for 2026-2028 that would position EngageMedia to be more effective and optimal in addressing significant challenges and issues in South and Southeast Asia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EngageMedia &#xe4;r en ideell organisation som fr&#xe4;mjar digitala r&#xe4;ttigheter, &#xf6;ppen och s&#xe4;ker teknik, och dokument&#xe4;rer om sociala fr&#xe5;gor. EngageMedia st&#xf6;djer f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsakt&#xf6;rer i Asien och Oceanien och globalt genom att kombinerar video, teknik, kunskap och n&#xe4;tverk f&#xf6;r att driva &#xf6;nskv&#xe4;rd f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring inom demokrati, m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, och milj&#xf6;. I samarbete med olika n&#xe4;tverk och r&#xf6;relser bidrar EngageMedia till att f&#xf6;rsvara och fr&#xe4;mja digitala r&#xe4;ttigheter.

Den f&#xf6;reslagna budgeten &#xe4;r totalt 2 166 100 USD, vilket motsvarar cirka 23 000 000 SEK f&#xf6;r 3 &#xe5;r (&#xe5;r 1: 1 660 642 USD, &#xe5;r 2: 745 666 USD och &#xe5;r 3: 759 791 USD). EngageMedias analys visar att r&#xf6;relser som fr&#xe4;mjar m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter i Asien och Oceanien arbetar mot en bakgrund av storskalig desinformation, &#xf6;kand auktorit&#xe4;rism, intensifierad &#xf6;vervakning, &#xf6;kad censur och  v&#xe5;ldsbejakande extremism. Dessa faktorer f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;rras ytterligare av oreglerad maskininl&#xe4;rning, anv&#xe4;ndandet av cybers&#xe4;kerhetslagar som vapen, och svagare demokratiska institutioner. Dessa fr&#xe5;gor addresseras i EngageMedias projektf&#xf6;rslag.  F&#xf6;r att motverka digital auktorit&#xe4;rism och ett krympande civilt utrymme s&#xe5;  s&#xf6;ker EngageMedia st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att bidra till:

1) &#xd6;kade grundl&#xe4;ggande friheter f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsakt&#xf6;rer och filmskapare som driver klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa och digitala r&#xe4;ttigheter; 2) St&#xf6;rre f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else hos civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer (CSOs) f&#xf6;r att engagera sig i policyutveckling och s&#xe4;rskilt motverka desinformation, bidra till ett &#xf6;kat plattformsansvar och AI-styrning (det vill s&#xe4;ga de regler, principer och standarder som s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;ller att AI-teknik utvecklas och anv&#xe4;nds p&#xe5; ett ansvarsfullt s&#xe4;tt); 3) St&#xe4;rkt solidaritet mellan de CSOs som arbetar f&#xf6;r digitala r&#xe4;ttigheter; samt 4) &#xd6;kad s&#xe4;kerhet f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nniskor&#xe4;ttsf&#xf6;rsvarare genom antagande och utveckling av &#xf6;ppen och s&#xe4;ker teknik.
EngageMedia efterfr&#xe5;gar ocks&#xe5; st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att utveckla och implementera en uppdaterad strategi f&#xf6;r 2026-2028, vilken skulle positionera EngageMedia i att effektivt  addresera de betydande utmaningar som ses i  i Syd- och Sydostasien.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives of the programme 2024-2027

The overall objective of the programme is in alignment with EngageMedia&apos;s vision and mission as outlined in the current strategic plan. EngageMedia envisions human rights, democracy and the environment are respected by businesses and Asia-Pacific governments. CSO meaningfully participates in meeting social and environmental challenges. 

2022-2025 Objective 1: Strengthen networks and platforms for digital rights, open and secure technology and video for change practitioners, fostering collaboration, engagement, campaigning, and mobilization. 
2022-2025 Objective 2: Strengthen changemakers&apos; knowledge, skills, and resources in effective communications and advocacy, digital rights, open and secure technologies, and video for change
2022-2025 Objective 3: Increase EngageMedias organizational effectiveness by developing its systems for communications, technology, sustainability, leadership, management, governance, learning, and team developments

Under these strategic objectives, EngageMedia seeks support to contribute to: 
1) Greater freedoms for changeseekers, changemakers and filmmakers for climate justice and digital rights 2) Greater understanding for civil society organizations (CSOs) to engage in public
policy development, particularly in countering disinformation, platform accountability, and AI governance 3) Greater solidarity among digital rights CSOs and 4) Greater security for human rights defenders through the adoption and development of open and secure technologies.</narrative>
  </description>
